};
---

<Layout
  title="Maine Dispensary Directory: Find a Local Guide by Town"
  description="Browse 61 Maine city, town, and regional dispensary guides with local market notes, map search links, and internal guide links."
  heroImage="/images/heroes/find-a-dispensary.jpg"
  article={{ author: "Steve Kelly", authorId: "steve-kelly", authorTitle: "Founder & Publisher", publishDate: "2026-01-10", modifiedDate: "2026-05-14", section: "Reference" }}
>
  <style>
    .directory-header { text-align: center; margin-bottom: 4rem; }
    .hero-badge { display: inline-block; background: var(--color-accent); color: var(--color-background); padding: 0.5rem 1rem; border-radius: 2rem; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.1em; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    .lead { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--color-text-light); max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; }
    .market-overview { background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--color-border); border-radius: 2rem; padding: 3rem; margin-bottom: 5rem; }
    .market-overview h2 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--color-primary); margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    .market-overview p { font-size: 1rem; color: var(--color-text-light); line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
    .market-overview p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .region-directory { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4.5rem; margin-bottom: 6rem; }
    .region-section h2 { margin: 0 0 1.5rem; padding-bottom: 1rem; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--color-border); font-family: var(--font-serif); font-size: 2rem; color: var(--color-primary); }
    .guide-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 1.25rem; }
    .guide-card { background: var(--color-surface); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 1.25rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.02); }
    .guide-card h3 { margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0.75rem; font-family: var(--font-serif); color: var(--color-primary); }
    .guide-card p { color: var(--color-text-light); line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1.25rem; }
    .guide-actions { display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .btn-map, .btn-guide { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-height: 2.5rem; padding: 0.65rem 0.85rem; border-radius: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.85rem; }
    .btn-guide { background: var(--color-primary); color: var(--color-background); }
    .btn-map { border: 1px solid var(--color-primary); color: var(--color-primary); }
    [data-theme="dark"] .guide-card, [data-theme="dark"] .market-overview { background: var(--color-surface); }
    /* OCP-licensed cities section (compact list of additional towns w/ retail access) */
    .ocp-section { margin-top: 4rem; padding-top: 3rem; border-top: 2px solid var(--color-border); }
    .ocp-intro, .ocp-source { color: var(--color-text-light); line-height: 1.7; max-width: 760px; }
    .ocp-source { font-size: 0.875rem; margin-top: 0.5rem; }
    .ocp-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
    .ocp-card { background: var(--color-surface); padding: 1.25rem; border-radius: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); }
    .ocp-card h3 { margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-size: 1.0625rem; font-family: var(--font-serif); color: var(--color-primary); display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .ocp-tag { font-size: 0.6875rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; padding: 0.125rem 0.5rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; font-family: var(--font-sans); }
    .ocp-tag.au { background: var(--color-primary); color: var(--color-background); }
    .ocp-tag.med { background: rgba(88, 129, 87, 0.15); color: var(--color-primary); }
    .ocp-count { font-size: 0.875rem; color: var(--color-text-light); margin: 0 0 0.5rem; font-weight: 600; }
    .ocp-sample { font-size: 0.8125rem; color: var(--color-text-light); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; line-height: 1.5; font-style: italic; }
    .ocp-actions { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .ocp-actions .btn-map, .ocp-actions .btn-guide-secondary { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; min-height: 2.25rem; padding: 0.5rem 0.75rem; border-radius: 0.5rem; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; font-size: 0.8125rem; }
    .ocp-actions .btn-map { border: 1px solid var(--color-primary); color: var(--color-primary); }
    .ocp-actions .btn-guide-secondary { background: transparent; border: 1px solid var(--color-border); color: var(--color-text); }
  </style>

  <section class="directory-header">
    <div class="hero-badge">{allGuides.length} Curated Local Guides + {ocpCities.filter(c => !allGuideNames.has(c.n.toLowerCase())).length} OCP-Licensed Towns</div>
    <h1>Find a Maine Dispensary Guide by Town or City</h1>
    <p class="lead">Use this directory to jump into the local guide for each Maine town, city, or region where Maine Dispensary Guide has published coverage. Every card links to a real guide page and a map search for that local market.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="market-overview">
    <h2>Maine's Dispensary Landscape</h2>
    <p>Maine's cannabis market is local and uneven: Greater Portland, York County, the Sebago corridor, western mountain towns, and midcoast communities each behave differently. This page is a guide index, not a paid store ranking, so it avoids dead menu CTAs and points readers toward the local context pages that already exist.</p>
    <p>Use the guide links for editorial context and the map links for live location searches. Store hours, menus, and licensing status can change; verify directly before visiting.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="region-directory">
    {guideRegions.map((region) => (
      <section class="region-section" aria-labelledby={`region-${region.name.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-')}`}>
        <h2 id={`region-${region.name.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9]+/g, '-')}`}>{region.name}</h2>
        <div class="guide-grid">
          {region.guides.map((guide) => (
            <article class="guide-card">
              <h3>{guide.name}</h3>
              <p>{guide.summary}</p>
              <div class="guide-actions">
                <a href={guide.href} class="btn-guide">Read guide</a>
                <a href={guide.mapUrl} class="btn-map" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Map search</a>
              </div>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    ))}
  </div>

  <Callout title="Own or operate a Maine dispensary?" type="tip">
    If your local guide needs an update, use the <a href="/contact">contact form</a> with the town, license name, and source link. We prioritize corrections that can be verified against public records or operator-owned pages.
  </Callout>

  <section class="ocp-section" aria-labelledby="ocp-region">
    <h2 id="ocp-region">All OCP-Licensed Maine Cities ({ocpAuCities.length + ocpMedCities.length} additional towns)</h2>
    <p class="ocp-intro">Maine Dispensary Guide publishes a curated local guide for the highest-traffic towns. Below are the {ocpAuCities.length + ocpMedCities.length} additional Maine towns with at least one active adult-use store or caregiver storefront licensed by the Maine Office of Cannabis Policy. Each row links to a map search and the OCP licensee search for that town. <strong>Recently added full guides:</strong> <a href="/guides/bath-dispensary-guide">Bath</a>, <a href="/guides/brewer-dispensary-guide">Brewer</a>, <a href="/guides/berwick-dispensary-guide">Berwick</a>. Local guides for other towns are in the editorial queue; submit your town as a <a href="/contact">suggested guide</a> if you want it prioritized.</p>
    <p class="ocp-source">Source: <a href="https://www.maine.gov/dafs/ocp/open-data/adult-use/licensee-search" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OCP Adult-Use Licensee CSV (April 2026)</a> + <a href="https://www11.maine.gov/dafs/ocp/open-data/medical-use/registrant-search" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OCP Medical Registrant CSV (April 2026)</a>. {ocpAuCities.length} towns have adult-use retail access, {ocpMedCities.length} have medical caregiver storefronts only.</p>
    <div class="ocp-grid">
      {[...ocpAuCities, ...ocpMedCities].sort((a, b) => a.n.localeCompare(b.n)).map((city) => (
        <article class="ocp-card">
          <h3>
            {city.n}
            {city.t === 'au' ? <span class="ocp-tag au">Adult-Use</span> : <span class="ocp-tag med">Caregiver</span>}
          </h3>
          <p class="ocp-count">{city.c} active {city.t === 'au' ? `store${city.c > 1 ? 's' : ''}` : `caregiver storefront${city.c > 1 ? 's' : ''}`}</p>
          {city.s && city.s.length > 0 && <p class="ocp-sample">{city.s.slice(0, 2).join(' · ')}</p>}
          <div class="ocp-actions">
            <a href={`https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=${encodeURIComponent(city.n + ', ME cannabis')}`} class="btn-map" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Map search</a>
            <a href="https://www.maine.gov/dafs/ocp/open-data/adult-use/licensee-search" class="btn-guide-secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">OCP search</a>
          </div>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(directoryJsonLd)}></script>
